<pdd-reason>Exposes local ordinary-language intent planning and exactly approved application as `pdd intent plan` and `pdd intent apply` for humans and AI harnesses.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "cli",
  "cli": {
    "commands": [
      {
        "name": "intent plan",
        "description": "Plan an ordinary-language request against local project evidence without changing files or requiring GitHub"
      },
      {
        "name": "intent apply",
        "description": "Apply the exact approved local intent plan through durable intent, prompt, story, test, and sync workflows without requiring GitHub"
      }
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>

<pdd-dependency>intent_python.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-dependency>intent_apply_python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

% You are an expert Python engineer. Write `pdd/commands/intent.py`.

<include>context/python_preamble.prompt</include>

% Role & Scope
  Implement a thin Click command group over `pdd.intent` and
  `pdd.intent_apply`. The command is an
  agent-facing front door, although it must also be understandable when a human
  runs it.

<vocabulary>
- Correct: the literal `--kind correct` enum value for a new event that supersedes a prior local intent because its accepted meaning was wrong.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 - Command surface
Expose a `@click.group(name="intent")` named `intent_cli` with `plan` and
`apply` subcommands. `pdd intent --help` MUST state that the group accepts
ordinary product intent and handles PDD routing. `pdd intent plan --help` MUST
state that planning is local, requires no GitHub issue, and changes no project
files. `pdd intent apply --help` MUST state that it mutates the scoped project
after exact plan approval and requires no GitHub issue.

R2 - Input forms
Both subcommands MUST accept exactly one input form: `--text
<ordinary-language request>`, positional `SOURCE` naming an existing local text
file, or piped standard input when neither `SOURCE` nor `--text` is supplied.
Reject simultaneous `SOURCE` and `--text`, missing interactive input,
unreadable/non-file sources, empty input, and input larger than 100,000
characters with clear Click errors.

R3 - Project and title options
Support optional `--project-root <directory>` (default current directory) and
`--title <human title>`. `--project-root` MAY name a proposed new directory
that does not exist yet; planning MUST NOT create it and apply MAY create it
only after exact approval. Resolve the project root before calling
`build_intent_plan`. Do not require a GitHub URL, prompt path, internal target
name, story slug, output path, or PDD configuration knowledge.

R4 - Output modes
Default output MUST be `render_review_card(plan)`. `--json` MUST instead emit
only deterministic JSON from `intent_plan_to_dict(plan)`, with indentation and
sorted object keys suitable for an AI harness. Do not mix status prose into
JSON stdout.

R5 - Planning-only truthfulness
The `plan` command MUST NOT write any project files, call GitHub, invoke an LLM,
generate stories/tests/code, or run synchronization. It MUST never imply that
the request was applied. Errors exit non-zero.

R6 - Apply approval and agent options
`intent apply` MUST require `--approve <intent-id>` and rebuild the same plan
from the exact supplied request/root/title/source before calling
`apply_intent`. Support agent-facing `--kind
[add|clarify|correct|remove|replace]`, `--supersedes <intent-id>`,
`--characterized`, `--no-story`, and `--no-sync`. The brownfield help MUST say
that `--characterized` asserts tests were actually run. These are mechanical
agent options, not questions the product human must answer.
Support `--approve-story <sha256>` for the second approval gate. The agent MUST
present the generated story's meaning before passing that hash.

R7 - Apply output and exit
Default apply output MUST use a concise human renderer.
`--json` MUST emit only `intent_apply_result_to_dict` as indented,
sorted-key JSON. A failed result MUST exit nonzero after emitting its report.
An `awaiting_story_approval` result MUST exit 2 so a harness can distinguish it
from a workflow failure. Do not mix child-process output into JSON stdout.
</contract_rules>

% Deliverables
- Code: `pdd/commands/intent.py`
- Tests: `tests/commands/test_pdd_commands_intent.py`
